### Read phase
Single-client range: ~10.6s for 226 K records. Throttles up to 8/s at 16 clients with ~1.9–2.0s P50 latency.

### Mixed phase
~20 ops/s peak (inserts + ranges). Reads still dominate, stalling inserts.

### Tail phase
~211 ops/s peak at 10 clients (190 inserts/s + 21 ranges/s).

## Flamegraph (write-heavy workload)
- **Compaction**: ~26 % CPU (down from 66.7 % in earlier runs)
- **Blocking pool**: ~76 % (idle/parked most of the time, compaction when active)
- **Tokio runtime**: ~13 % (server I/O + insert path)
- **Record sorting**: ~5 %
- **Allocation**: ~5 %
- **fsync**: <1 % (once per second → negligible)

## Key improvements over previous runs
1. Write throughput **+47 %** peak (83.3K → 122.6K)
2. P50 latency **−38 %** (5.97ms → 3.67ms)  
3. P99 latency **−46 %** (15.37ms → 8.29ms)
4. Compaction CPU **−61 %** (66.7 % → 26 %)

## Takeaways
- Timer-based fsync almost eliminates sync overhead
- 32 MB memtable keeps flush rate low → stable SST count (9–21)
- Compaction no longer the dominant bottleneck
- **Reads are now the main performance problem** (range scans merge across many SSTs)
